+# Glossary
+
+- **Normalised email** — an email after `normalize_email`: trimmed and lower-cased. The
+  identity of a contact; the repository keys on it.
+- **Import** — loading a CSV file (same columns as the CSV export) into a repository with
+  `import_contacts`. See `specs/csv-import.md`.
+- **Contact row** — a non-blank data line of an import file. Blank rows (all cells empty) are
+  skipped and do not count towards the 1000-row limit.
+- **Row number** — the file line a row starts on; the header is row 1, the first contact row 2,
+  blank lines included.
+- **Merge** — what an import does to an existing contact: name replaced, phone replaced only
+  by a non-blank valid value, tags added. An import never removes data. See ADR 0001.
+- **Import error** — a row problem that makes the import skip the whole row (bad name, email
+  or tag; duplicate email in the file; too many cells).
+- **Import warning** — a row problem that the import works around and reports; currently only
+  an invalid phone, which is left unchanged.
+- **File error** — `ImportFileError`: the file as a whole cannot be imported (bad encoding,
+  missing required column, empty, over 1000 contact rows); nothing is imported.
