+# 0001 — CSV import merges into existing contacts and never removes data
+
+Date: 2026-10-29 · Status: accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Sales imports spreadsheets of leads. Their files often lack phone numbers or carry only some
+of a contact's tags, and phones in them are frequently malformed. Treating a row as the full
+truth about a contact would silently wipe data we already hold.
+
+## Decision
+
+- An import row for an existing email updates that contact (never a second one).
+- The name from the file replaces the stored name.
+- The phone is replaced only by a non-blank, valid value. A blank cell keeps the stored phone;
+  an invalid phone keeps it too and is reported as a warning, while the rest of the row is
+  still applied.
+- Tags from the file are added; an import never removes tags.
+- Import is partial: a row with an error is skipped entirely, other rows are applied. Only
+  file-level problems (`ImportFileError`) abort the whole import, leaving the repository
+  unchanged.
+- Within one file, the first row for an email wins; later rows with that email are errors.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- An import cannot be used to clear phones or remove tags; that needs the regular use cases.
+- Future import sources (other formats, an HTTP upload) should follow the same merge rules.
