+# CSV import
+
+## What and why
+
+Sales keeps leads in spreadsheets and wants to load a whole CSV file into contactbook
+instead of adding contacts one by one. The import reads a file with the same columns as
+our CSV export (`name,email,phone,tags`, tags joined with `;`), creates new contacts,
+merges into existing ones, and returns a report saying what happened to every row so the
+sender can fix the bad rows and re-import.
+
+Importing is additive: it never loses data we already hold. A bad phone number must not
+cost us a contact, so it is a warning, not an error.
+
+## Interface (fixed by the requester, verbatim)
+
+- `src/contactbook/importer.py`: `import_contacts(repo: InMemoryContactRepository, data: str | bytes) -> ImportReport`
+  where `data` is the file content: raw bytes as read from disk, or already-decoded text.
+- `ImportReport` (dataclass, same module): `created: list[str]`, `updated: list[str]` (normalised
+  emails), `errors: list[RowIssue]`, `warnings: list[RowIssue]`.
+- `RowIssue` (dataclass, same module): `row: int`, `column: str | None`, `message: str`.
+- `ImportFileError(ContactError)` in `src/contactbook/errors.py`, raised when the file as a whole
+  can't be imported.
+
+`ImportFileError` is also exported from the `contactbook` package.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+### Decoding
+
+- [ ] `bytes` input is decoded as UTF-8; a leading UTF-8 BOM is accepted and ignored.
+- [ ] `str` input that starts with the BOM character `﻿` is accepted; the BOM is ignored
+      (the first header column is still recognised).
+- [ ] `bytes` that are not valid UTF-8 raise `ImportFileError` whose message tells the user to
+      re-save the file as "CSV UTF-8".
+- [ ] Only comma is a delimiter.
+
+### Header and file-level rejection
+
+- [ ] The first line of the file is the header. Columns may appear in any order; header names
+      are matched case-insensitively, ignoring surrounding whitespace.
+- [ ] `email` is a required column. The name comes from a `name` column, or, if there is
+      none, from the pair `first_name` + `last_name` (both columns required), joined with one
+      space and then validated like any name (so a blank `last_name` gives just the first name).
+      If both `name` and the pair are present, `name` is used.
+- [ ] `phone` and `tags` are optional columns. Other columns are ignored silently.
+- [ ] A missing required column raises `ImportFileError`; the repository is unchanged.
+- [ ] Empty input (no content, or only whitespace) raises `ImportFileError`.
+- [ ] Malformed CSV (e.g. an unterminated quote) raises `ImportFileError` rather than reading
+      the rest of the file into one cell.
+- [ ] A header-only file returns an empty report (all four lists empty).
+- [ ] More than 1000 contact rows (blank rows not counted) raises `ImportFileError` and nothing
+      is imported. Exactly 1000 is accepted.
+- [ ] Whenever `ImportFileError` is raised, the repository is unchanged.
+
+### Row numbering and blank rows
+
+- [ ] `RowIssue.row` is the file line on which the row starts: the header is row 1, the first
+      contact is row 2, and every line counts, blank lines included.
+- [ ] A row whose cells are all empty or whitespace is skipped silently (no error, no warning).
+- [ ] A row with fewer cells than the header has its missing cells treated as empty.
+
+### Validation of a row
+
+All values are normalised with the existing validators (`Contact.create` / `validation.py`).
+
+- [ ] An invalid or blank email is an error with column `email`.
+- [ ] An invalid or blank name is an error with column `name` (also for a
+      `first_name`/`last_name` file).
+- [ ] An invalid tag is an error with column `tags`. The tags cell is split on `;`; empty
+      parts (e.g. a trailing `;`) are ignored.
+- [ ] A row with more cells than the header is an error with column `None`.
+- [ ] A row with an error is skipped entirely: nothing from it is applied, also not partly to
+      an existing contact, and its email appears in neither `created` nor `updated`.
+- [ ] An invalid phone is **not** an error: the rest of the row is imported or merged, the phone
+      is left as it was (none for a new contact), and a warning with column `phone` is added
+      for that row. The bad phone is the only kind of warning.
+- [ ] `RowIssue.column` is always one of `name`, `email`, `phone`, `tags` or `None`.
+
+### Duplicates within the file
+
+- [ ] Emails are compared after normalisation (case and surrounding whitespace ignored).
+- [ ] The first row with a given email wins. Every later row with the same email is an error
+      with column `None` whose message names the first row's number, and is not applied.
+      This holds even if the first row was itself rejected for another error: the file is
+      ambiguous about that contact, so none of its rows is applied.
+
+### Creating and merging
+
+- [ ] A row whose email is not in the repository creates a contact; its normalised email is
+      appended to `created`.
+- [ ] A row whose email is already in the repository updates that contact (never a second
+      contact); its normalised email is appended to `updated`, even if nothing changed.
+- [ ] On update the name from the file replaces the stored name.
+- [ ] On update a non-blank, valid phone replaces the stored phone; a blank phone cell (or no
+      `phone` column) keeps the stored phone.
+- [ ] On update the tags from the file are added to the stored tags; an import never removes a
+      tag.
+- [ ] `created` and `updated` list emails in file order; `errors` and `warnings` are in row
+      order.
+- [ ] A file produced by `export_csv` imports back into an empty repository as the same
+      contacts.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Encodings other than UTF-8 (no Latin-1 / cp1252 detection) and delimiters other than comma.
+- Deleting contacts or removing tags or phones through an import.
+- A `ContactBook` method for import; persistence adapters or HTTP endpoints.
+- All-or-nothing import on row errors (only file-level errors abort the whole import).
+- Defined behaviour for duplicate header names.
+
+## Scope limits
+
+- New module `src/contactbook/importer.py`, new error in `errors.py`, export in `__init__.py`,
+  tests in `tests/test_importer.py`, a line in the README layout. Standard library only.
